BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:97c1f765df14a353b1f2e69deb02207ca31d2d4ad0a16be4f58b29442784e0c0@pruts-
 agenda.local
X-PRUTS-SOURCE:thehmm
X-PRUTS-UUID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl
X-PRUTS-RADAR-ID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl
X-PRUTS-OCCURRENCE-ID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl:2026-12-
 11T19:00:00+01:00
DTSTAMP:20261127T055701Z
SUMMARY:Suggested For You: 10 Years of The Hmm
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261211T180000Z
DTEND:20261212T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Earlier this year\, the internet was briefly filled with the ho
 pe that 2026 might become the new 2016. In quasi-historical fashion\, user
 s resurfaced early Instagram filters and interfaces\, Tumblr-motivational
  quotes\, old memes\, and other fragments of a supposedly simpler internet
 . Collectively\, it became a meditation on how social media used to be bet
 ter\, or at least how much it felt better. Though users relied on a more g
 eneralised nostalgia to resurrect the aesthetic of the time\, they were\,
  in a sense\, correct. The internet really did feel different. 2016 was th
 e year that all news feeds became algorithmic\, and with it our relationsh
 ip with social media fundamentally changed.\n\nSerendipitously\, The Hmm w
 as also born ten years ago\, in 2016. Since then\, we have tried to trace\
 , interrogate and intervene in the forces shaping our online lives\, inclu
 ding the algorithmic feed itself. To celebrate this legacy\, we are throwi
 ng a festive evening at W139 in Amsterdam\, filled with performances\, wor
 kshops\, drinks and more.\n‎\n‎Suggested For You: Reflecting on a deca
 de in the feed\nThe evening will also mark the launch of our 10-year anniv
 ersary publication: Suggested For You: Reflecting on a Decade in the Feed.
  Part celebration\, part reflection\, the book looks back at the algorithm
 ic feed and the decade of internet cultures that has unfolded around it. F
 eaturing essays\, interviews\, image contributions and artist profiles fro
 m Ruba Al-Sweel\, Evelyn Austin and Rejo Zenger\, Jak Ritger\, Soyun Park
  and Leo Scarin\, Noura Tafeche\, Neema Githere\, Alex Quicho\, Constant D
 ullaart\, Mamali Shafahi and Ali Eslami\, Danielle Brathwaite-Shirley\, K
  Allado McDowell and Aidan Walker\, the publication brings together a rang
 e of perspectives on how the algorithmic feed has come to shape life onlin
 e.\nYou can already pre-order the book! It will be available to pick-up an
 d purchase at the event.\n‎\nProgram\n19.00–22.00 at W139 \n\nClassic
  5-minute talks by members of The Hmm team and board\n\nThe launch of our
  book Suggested For You\n\nAlgodance\, an interactive installation by Mari
 t Hoefsloot and Julie van Essen\n\nThe Hmm’s Hotline\, to share your tho
 ughts and questions on our theme for next year\n\nMake Your Own Slopject\,
  ongoing workshop\n\n\n22.00–1.00 at Bar San Francisco \n\nPerformance l
 ecture by Macarena Magaña Villar\nLive set by Jochem Joost\nDj sets by ju
 stin case & jujulove\n\n\n\nWhat you need to know\n📅 Date: Friday 11 De
 cember 2026\n🕗 Times: 19.00–1.00 CET\n📍 Location: from 19:00–22:
 00 at W139\, Warmoesstraat 139\, 1012 JB Amsterdam & from 22:00–1:00 at
  Bar San Francisco\, Zeedijk 40\, 1012 AZ Amsterdam\n🎟 Tickets: Free\,
  but please register! \n\n‎\n\n‎💚 This programme is kindly supporte
 d by the Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industry\, Amsterdams Fonds voor de K
 unst and Het Cultuurfonds. The publication Suggested For You is supported
  by Mondriaanfonds.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/celebrating-10-years-of-the-hmm-book-launch/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
